    pr_ref:  # 845e
    description: ""  # 845e
    fields:  # 845e
      statement: "python.yaml rows platform.architecture under host_info_read. platform.py:720 calls _syscmd_file(executable, ...) with executable defaulting to sys.executable; _syscmd_file is documented as Interface to the system file command and runs subprocess.check_output with argv file -b TARGET. A row that launches a subprocess catalogued as a host-info read means the subprocess boundary is never seen at that call site."  # 845e
      root_cause: "Boundary chosen from the module's purpose (platform = host description) rather than from the function's implementation, which shells out."  # 845e
